cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this work, cite it, and cite the MaleCNS v1.0 release it depends
  on. Take the canonical citation for MaleCNS from the publisher record at the
  DOI below; the entry here carries the identifier only, not a transcribed
  author list.
title: "fly-balatro: the MaleCNS connectome as a frozen reservoir playing Balatro"
abstract: >-
  The complete male Drosophila connectome (MaleCNS v1.0), brain-only, run as a
  frozen leaky integrate-and-fire network that plays Balatro. Poker hand
  analysis is computed outside the brain and relayed in as an odour on 32
  olfactory glomeruli; the action is then produced either by a trained readout
  on spike counts, or with no trained action readout at all, by the fly's own
  mushroom-body output neurons under dopamine-gated KC-to-MBON depression driven
  by the chips the game pays. Includes a degree-, weight- and subtype-preserving
  rewiring control of the antennal-lobe-to-Kenyon-cell calyx, a preregistered
  2x2 plasticity experiment, and the fly clearing ante 1 of the real Steam game
  through a mod.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Poluri
    given-names: Abhiram
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-14"
keywords:
  - connectomics
  - Drosophila
  - MaleCNS
  - mushroom body
  - reservoir computing
  - synaptic plasticity
